# Keep secrets and local cruft OUT of the container image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file a local
# `docker build` bakes backend/.env — containing the real JWT_SECRET and the
# BigQuery key path — into every published image layer, readable by anyone who
# can pull it. Runtime config comes from Cloud Run env vars, never from a
# committed/copied .env, so excluding it changes nothing about how the app runs.
.env
.env.*
*-credentials.local.txt
*.json.key
bq-*.json

# Local caches / build noise
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore
